# BAS S-ClsBot / I-Case3: Constructor match arms with disjoint variant tags.
# [try [fn [] 42]] returns Variant(Result.Ok, Int(42)). The I-Case3 rule in infer_match
# accumulates negations: after the [Result.Ok v] arm, remaining_scrutinee gains ~"Result.Ok"
# via Type::Negation. S-ClsBot: Intersection([scrutinee, "Result.Ok"]) ∩ ~"Result.Ok" = Never.
# The [Result.Error _] arm correctly matches an uninhabited scrutinee type.
[result: [try [fn [] 42]]
 value: [match result
   [case [let v] [Result.Ok v]    v]
   [Result.Error _]:              0]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Variant(Result.Ok, Int(42)), "value": Int(42)})
